# thoth_policy

```terraform
resource "thoth_policy" "hold_deletes" {
  environment = "dev"
  name        = "Hold deletes"
  type        = "scope"
  enforcement = "review"
  applied_to  = ["all"]

  rules_json = jsonencode({
    conditions = {
      action_class = ["delete"]
    }
  })
}
```

A rule lives in one environment. Changing `environment` replaces it; to move a dev rule to
prod, promote it with the configuration preview (`preview_policy_rule`) or the API.

With an org admin's key a new rule starts active. Otherwise it starts `pending` until an org admin
approves it, and `status` shows that; Terraform never approves a rule. `enabled = false` turns a
rule off, and turning it back on needs an org admin's key.

Import with `environment/policy_id`:

```shell
terraform import thoth_policy.hold_deletes dev/6ae1441907c1c31e7e44ca5a
```

